{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112026","id":2946919348,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6vpmu0","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112026","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112026.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/112026.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112026","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112026/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/112026/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112026/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/d180b9af9f64c84da7a48a45e60615ee5916d427","number":112026,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Use more practical default plural rules","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I recently discovered that the current default plural rules for `fr` specify three plural forms for French. However, most gettext-related tools, including Weblate, assume that French has only two plural forms. The same also happens to some other languages, e.g., Portuguese and Spanish.\r\n\r\nIt seems that the third plural form is for messages like this:\r\n\r\n- 1 page\r\n- 2 pages\r\n- 1M de pages\r\n\r\nI'm not sure how widely this approach has been adopted. However, from a practical standpoint, I think we should try to align our the default behavior with gettext-related tools as much as possible to avoid breaking certain expectations.\r\n\r\nI took a look at how `msginit` picks the plural rule for the `Plural-Forms` field:\r\n\r\n- If available, use the plural rule specified in the [gettext documentation](https://www.gnu.org/software/gettext/manual/html_node/Plural-forms.html). Data organized in [this table](https://cgit.git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/gettext.git/tree/gettext-tools/src/plural-table.c).\r\n- Call `cldr-plurals` to look up and convert plural rules from the [Unicode CLDR](https://cldr.unicode.org/) database ([plurals.xml](https://github.com/unicode-org/cldr/blob/main/common/supplemental/plurals.xml)).\r\n- If none of the above methods work, leave it blank.\r\n\r\nFollowing these steps, I wrote a script to generate the `plural_rules` array.\r\n\r\n<details><summary><code>gen_plural_rules.py</code></summary>\r\n\r\n```python\r\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\r\nimport re\r\nimport subprocess\r\nimport sys\r\nimport xml.etree.ElementTree as ET\r\n\r\n\r\ndef parse_plurals_xml(path: str) -> set[str]:\r\n    locales: set[str] = set()\r\n    tree = ET.parse(path)\r\n    for pr in tree.findall('.//pluralRules'):\r\n        locale_list = pr.attrib.get('locales').strip()\r\n        if not locale_list:\r\n            continue\r\n        for loc in locale_list.split():\r\n            locales.add(loc)\r\n    return locales\r\n\r\n\r\ndef parse_plural_table_c(path: str) -> dict[str, str]:\r\n    mapping: dict[str, str] = {}\r\n    pattern = re.compile(r'^\\s*\\{\\s*\"([^\"]+)\"\\s*,\\s*\"[^\"]*\"\\s*,\\s*\"([^\"]*)\"\\s*\\},?')\r\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\r\n        for line in f:\r\n            m = pattern.match(line)\r\n            if not m:\r\n                continue\r\n            loc = m.group(1)\r\n            rule = m.group(2)\r\n            mapping[loc] = rule\r\n    return mapping\r\n\r\n\r\ndef get_cldr_plurals(locales: set[str], plurals_xml: str) -> dict[str, str]:\r\n    if not locales:\r\n        return {}\r\n\r\n    candidates = [\r\n        \"cldr-plurals\",\r\n        \"/usr/lib/gettext/cldr-plurals\",\r\n    ]\r\n    cldr_exe: str | None = None\r\n    for cmd in candidates:\r\n        try:\r\n            subprocess.check_call([cmd, \"--version\"], stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL)\r\n            cldr_exe = cmd\r\n            break\r\n        except Exception:\r\n            continue\r\n    if not cldr_exe:\r\n        raise RuntimeError(\r\n            f\"cldr-plurals not found (tried: {', '.join(candidates)})\"\r\n        )\r\n\r\n    result: dict[str, str] = {}\r\n    for loc in locales:\r\n        try:\r\n            rule = subprocess.check_output([cldr_exe, loc, plurals_xml], text=True)\r\n            result[loc] = rule.strip()\r\n        except Exception as e:\r\n            sys.stderr.write(f\"cldr-plurals failed for {loc}: {e}\\n\")\r\n\r\n    return result\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main(plural_table_c: str, plurals_xml: str):\r\n    xml_locales = parse_plurals_xml(plurals_xml)\r\n    c_locale_to_rule = parse_plural_table_c(plural_table_c)\r\n\r\n    grouped = {}\r\n    for loc, rule in c_locale_to_rule.items():\r\n        grouped.setdefault(rule, []).append(loc)\r\n\r\n    missing = xml_locales - set(c_locale_to_rule.keys())\r\n    cldr_map = get_cldr_plurals(missing, plurals_xml)\r\n    for loc, rule in cldr_map.items():\r\n        grouped.setdefault(rule, []).append(loc)\r\n\r\n    print(\"static const char *plural_rules[][2] = {\")\r\n    for key in sorted(grouped.keys()):\r\n        locs = sorted(grouped[key])\r\n        locales_str = \" \".join(locs)\r\n        rule_str = key\r\n        print(f\"\\t{{ \\\"{locales_str}\\\", \\\"{rule_str}\\\" }},\")\r\n    print(\"\\t{ nullptr, nullptr }\")\r\n    print(\"};\")\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    plurals_xml = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) >= 2 else \"plurals.xml\"\r\n    plural_table_c = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) >= 3 else \"plural-table.c\"\r\n    main(plural_table_c, plurals_xml)\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\nIn this PR, I generated the `plural_rules` with the latest `plural-table.c` and `plurals.xml` from CLDR release 47.\r\n\r\nNote that starting with CLDR release 38, new plural rule syntax elements have been introduced for certain languages. Currently, gettext's `cldr-plurals` [does not](https://savannah.gnu.org/bugs/?func=detailitem&item_id=66378) support these, so no default plural rules are generated for `pt_PT`, `lld`, `scn`, and `vec`.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":8133949121,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAAB5NI2wQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:i18n","name":"topic:i18n","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12939969,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AxXLB","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/23","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/23/labels","number":23,"state":"closed","title":"4.6","d